        {
            "number": 5,
            "revision": "1b9c76e7ec029e51ee3ab191a49002359ba4ed85",
            "parents": [
                "b08bcdd03a8fc324e3494d59e6718dba79305fbb"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/16/84016/5",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Patrick NC Lin",
                "email": "patrick.nc.lin.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                "username": "PatrickLinww"
            },
            "createdOn": 1758790565,
            "author": {
                "name": "Patrick NC Lin",
                "email": "patrick.nc.lin.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                "username": "PatrickLinww"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick NC Lin",
                        "email": "patrick.nc.lin.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "PatrickLinww"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi @patrick@stwcx.xyz,\nI have uploaded an initial implementation based on this design.\nWhen convenient, please also review the corresponding code change here: https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-logging/+/85732"
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/runtime-debug-logging-enablement.md",
                    "line": 50,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "A systemd property is not something OpenBMC can approve.  Have you raised this upstream as a possibility?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/runtime-debug-logging-enablement.md",
                    "line": 50,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick NC Lin",
                        "email": "patrick.nc.lin.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "PatrickLinww"
                    },
                    "message": "I haven\u2019t proposed the new property to upstream yet. If this approach is unlikely to be accepted, would it make sense to add it in another suitable place instead?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/runtime-debug-logging-enablement.md",
                    "line": 78,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Aren't there changes necessary to phosphor-logging to support this?\n\nI'm not sure how the signal gets sent into each process to let the phosphor-logging library know to \"enable debug mode\".  We certainly don't want phosphor-logging to check `/run/systemd-debug-enabled` on each journal invocation.  How do we override the existing DEBUG_INVOCATION behavior for an already-running process?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/runtime-debug-logging-enablement.md",
                    "line": 78,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick NC Lin",
                        "email": "patrick.nc.lin.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "PatrickLinww"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes, phosphor-logging also needs to be modified to support this proposal. The main changes would be:\n1. Update send_debug_to_journal() so that it returns true when DEBUG_INVOCATION is unset or set to true, and returns false only when DEBUG_INVOCATION=0.\n2. Adjust the condition from `if (send_debug_to_journal || l != level::debug)` to `if (l != level::debug || (send_debug_to_journal && is_systemd_debug_enabled()))`\nThis leverages short-circuit evaluation so that there is no performance impact in normal cases. Only when debug-level logs are being processed will there be extra overhead.\n\nWith this approach, we no longer need to override DEBUG_INVOCATION. Instead, we can simply update .DebugEnable, which changes the return value of is_systemd_debug_enabled() to control whether debug-level logs are emitted."
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/runtime-debug-logging-enablement.md",
                    "line": 78,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick NC Lin",
                        "email": "patrick.nc.lin.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "PatrickLinww"
                    },
                    "message": "If checking `/run/systemd-debug-enabled` exist or not for every debug-level log is a concern, I think we could alternatively use shared memory?\n\nRegarding DEBUG_INVOCATION, if we want to update it at runtime, we would normally need to set the environment variable and restart the service for it to take effect. With this design, that step would no longer be necessary."
                }
            ],
